# SYNTHETIC macro. Invented targets, sample codes and motor positions; round
# fake energies. The COMMAND NAMES (`qdo`, `newfile`, `mv`, `mvr`, `trigger`,
# `IrL3_xas`) are the real SPEC and beamline command names, because a fixture
# that renamed them would exercise none of the reader's patterns — and a command
# name is not a scientific value, a sample identity or note prose.
#
# Reproduces: a macro declaring SEVERAL measurements (the real maximum is 8, in
# run15.mac), commands appearing BEFORE the first newfile declaration, and the
# documented four-argument acquisition call.
qdo Ir_XAS.mac

mv Sx -1.25 Sy 2.5 Sz -3.5

newfile 15_02_ZZ2_base_after1200Cycling_filter10_200mV

###      time/point         number of scans
IrL3_xas 0.5      2 		  1050       10
mvr Sz -0.3

###      time/point         number of scans
IrL3_xas 0.5      2 		  1050       10
mvr Sz -0.3

trigger

mv Sx -1.25 Sy 2.5 Sz -3.5

newfile 16_02_ZZ2_base_after1200Cycling_filter10_400mV

###      time/point         number of scans
IrL3_xas 0.5      2 		  1050       10
mvr Sz -0.3

trigger

#########################################################
######### CV steps ######################################
#########################################################

mv Sx -1.25 Sy 2.5 Sz -3.5

newfile 17_02_ZZ2_base_after1500Cycling_filter10_100mV

###      time/point         number of scans
IrL3_xas 0.5      3 		  1050       10
mvr Sz -0.3

trigger

# A call with the WRONG argument count. No real macro contains one; it is here
# because assigning four documented roles to three arguments by magnitude would
# be a guess, and the refusal path needs cover.
IrL3_xas 0.5 2 1050
